$ grep -rn 'retry fails in unit tests' test/

(no matches - the two tests that admitted to a live replay are gone)

Runtime confirmation: each rewritten test asserts a hit count on its
fake adapter (expect(retryAdapter.hits, ...)), which is only reachable
if the replay was served in-process.

$ grep -rn 'retryAdapter.hits' test/core/network test/integration/auth

test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_test.dart:179:          expect(retryAdapter.hits, 1);
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_test.dart:273:        expect(retryAdapter.hits, 2);
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:174:        expect(retryAdapter.hits, 0);
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:219:        expect(retryAdapter.hits, 3);
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:310:      expect(retryAdapter.hits, 0);
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:340:        expect(retryAdapter.hits, 1);
test/integration/auth/token_refresh_flow_test.dart:120:      expect(retryAdapter.hits, 1);

Three AuthInterceptor constructions above have no retryDioFactory:
ssl_pinning_test.dart:120/146/165 and api_client_interceptor_chain_test.dart
:201/270. None of them replays anything.

  - ssl_pinning_test only inspects adapters; no request is ever sent, and the
    replay client it builds delegates to the ApiClient adapter rather than
    opening a transport of its own.
  - api_client_interceptor_chain_test:201 scripts a 503 and :270 a 400, so the
    401 branch never runs; both point ApiClient.dio at the counting fake.

Wall clock for the whole suite is in criterion-7_network_suite.log: 206 tests
in ~11s, of which ~8s is the deliberate RetryInterceptor backoff in the 503
test. Nothing waits on a socket.
